 "findings": [
  "All four lanes (vanilla without speculative decoding, static, adaptive, eagle) write the same foreign token in 3/3 greedy repeats, with near-identical top-5 logprobs: the token comes from the target model, not from speculative decoding.",
  "At the position after '75.000.' / '541.500.' the model splits between ' beğen' (p~0.48-0.69) and end of turn (p~0.17-0.43); greedy picks ' beğen'.",
  "Removing the data-sufficiency rule from the prompt does not remove it (variant B).",
  "Rendering whole floats as integers in the answer table ('75000' instead of '75000.0'), with the original prompt, removes it for both questions (vanilla_integer_table).",
  "Not tested: whether the unquantized Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct shows the same behaviour (AWQ vs base model)."
 ],
